# Decide how to treat checks that do not apply: auth, A2A, WebMCP, DNS-AID, commerce

## Step

With the check list in hand, decide per non-applicable check whether the site serves an honest document (an A2A card that says what the MCP offers; OAuth discovery that says no auth), a deliberate 404 with the reason in `llms.txt`, or a DNS record in the Stack (DNS-AID). Level 5 must still hold, so the research asset says which of these the scanner requires. Commerce stays out of scope.
